## Research Scope
<!-- ID: research_scope -->
Wave 1 Track C covers runtime telemetry flow, reproducible latency measurements, daemon/log evidence, and bug-candidate isolation for the Scribe latency audit.

Boundaries:
- Research/RCA only; no source edits or fixes.
- Prefer direct Scribe/Council tool responses, current source, and daemon/log diagnostics over prose docs.
- Do not own deep storage implementation analysis; storage/Postgres internals are Track B/Sia's lane.
- Measurements must be non-destructive and bounded.

Startup evidence:
- `mcp__council_v2.open_session(persona_id="BugHunterAgent")` was exposed but failed because no Council profile exists for `bughunteragent`; session opening is therefore blocked for this persona in the current Council surface.
- `mcp__scribe.set_project(agent="BugHunterAgent", name="integrate-system-scribe-latency-20260616T050042Z", root="/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp")` succeeded and bound the active Scribe project.
- `mcp__scribe.read_recent(agent="BugHunterAgent", limit=10, project="integrate-system-scribe-latency-20260616T050042Z")` returned the current bracket context and prior baseline timing observations.


